{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1331670-perception-in-storypath","id":1331670,"title":"Perception in Storypath","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-19T17:01:39-07:00","id":1331670,"title":"Perception in Storypath","content":"Can someone point me towards how to manage the act of perception in Storypath (Scion, Trinity, Aberrant or other)<br /> <br /> The previous ways I know are<br /> <br /> 01. Attribute + Dedicated Skill<br /> WoD, Exalted<br /> <br /> 02. Attribute + Atribute (or subbing a Skill)<br /> CoD<br /> <br /> My assumption is that its Skill + Attribute most relevant similar to Initiative but I have nothing to back that up. Maybe relevant skill + cunning or composure <br /> <br /> Example while driving pilot + cunning or composure<br /> <br /> Thanks<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 08-19-2019, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T17:16:45-07:00","id":1331673,"title":"","content":"You are correct on your assumption.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s up to the situation. For detecting adversaries in the nature use Survival + Cunning, for detecting details on a piece of technology use Technology + Cunning, to detect details in the face of a person use Integrity + Cunning.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s basically you use the ability of dealing with people to detect details in people, ability of surviving in the wild to identify things in the wild, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T11:42:36-07:00","id":1333573,"title":"","content":"Would it be cunning or resolve? Doesn\u2019t resolve include attention to detail?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T12:49:09-07:00","id":1333584,"title":"","content":"Cunning is more about noticing details and fast thinking, while Resolve is more about mental endurance, keeping focus for longer periods is Resolve, but noticing the details is Cunning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T14:15:11-07:00","id":1333601,"title":"","content":"Attention to detail is in the definition of Resolve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T14:16:43-07:00","id":1333602,"title":"","content":"Cunning is the default perception Attribute because the game is assuming that you're rolling under stress and quick processing is essential (must the same that the CofD defaults to Wits for the same thing).<br /> <br /> Other Attributes can apply to perception if the SG feels it's appropriate. I would personally use Resolve instead of Cunning for something that's standing guard. As Mateus noted, a guard has to keep their mind sharp despite potentially long periods of nothing stimulating their minds, and thus their Resolve is easily more important than their Cunning. I'd likewise apply this to any sort of search where perseverance is more important than problem solving. Finding a needle in a haystack is just a matter of time and endurance.<br /> <br /> Swapping in Intelligence (something the book does mention in a few places) is appropriate when the consideration is more about linking data together. Investigating a crime scene for clues, especially without a strong time crunch, isn't just about noticing details quickly, but orienting how those details all relate to each other.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T14:20:27-07:00","id":1333603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1331670-perception-in-storypath?p=1333601#post1333601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attention to detail is in the definition of Resolve.</div> </div> </div> </div>The phrase &quot;attention to detail,&quot; is usually more a matter of personal habits than actual sensory skills. It implies a level of meticulous and exact manners when approaching a task, rather than quick thinking, literally sensing things, or problem solving. It's a &quot;slow and steady wins the race&quot; sort of mentality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}